<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Favila of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/739">739</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Fafila</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Favila was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 737 to 739, succeeding his father Pelagius. According to the Asturian chronicles he was killed by a bear while hunting, after only two years on the throne. He founded the church of Santa Cruz at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cangas-de-onis">Cangas de Onís</a>, whose dedication stone of 737 is one of the earliest records of the kingdom. The throne passed to his brother-in-law Alfonso I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/favila-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Favila of Asturias" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ecelan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monasterio_de_San_Pedro_de_Villanueva_-_Portada_-_Detalle01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Pelagius’s son and successor <b>Favila</b> was killed by a bear in 739, after only two years as king, according to the Asturian chronicles.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cangas-de-onis">Cangues d'Onís</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.35,-5.13&amp;year=729" aria-label="Cangues d'Onís on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4426 626 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Favila of Asturias"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4876 896h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4876 896h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=43.35,-5.13&amp;year=729">What was here in 729 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
